# Spec artifacts (quire-managed, not prettier-formatted)
spec/

# The agent-ix/qa-corpus submodule (agent-ix/quoin#237). Another repository's
# tree, pinned by SHA and read IN PLACE — `cd corpus/cases/<mode>/<case>/input
# && quire coverage --scope .` is the exact reproduction CI runs. Formatting it
# rewrites bytes quoin does not own, dirties the submodule working tree, and
# makes this repo's lint gate depend on qa-corpus's house style. Same reasoning
# as the two entries below: these bytes are evidence, not source. Landing the
# submodule without this entry left `make lint` red for three commits, two of
# which reported it clean.
corpus/

# Vendored quire output schemas (FR-029). These are copies of quire-rs's
# published artifacts and must match them BYTE FOR BYTE — their SHA-256 is
# recorded in src/quire/contract.ts and asserted on every test run. Formatting
# them locally rewrites the bytes and breaks the provenance check, which is
# exactly how a vendored contract drifts by default. Refresh them with
# scripts/refresh-quire-schemas.mjs, never with prettier.
src/quire/schemas/

# Real tool output, captured unedited (agent-ix/quoin#115). The ticket asked
# for the format decisions to be made "by reading real output from each tool,
# not from the spec of the format", so a fixture reformatted to house style is
# no longer the thing it was captured to be. Same reasoning as the vendored
# quire schemas above: these bytes are evidence, not source.
tests/fixtures/evidence/

# The agent-ix/quoin#164 coverage payload, captured unedited (quoin#379). The
# volume test asserts its exact length — `VOLUME_BYTES = 1_632_821` in
# rust/crates/quoin-quire/tests/volume.rs — so that a truncation or a
# line-ending rewrite on checkout fails loudly. Re-indenting it would move
# that number and turn the formatter into the authority on how large the
# incident payload was. Same rule as tests/fixtures/evidence/ above: these
# bytes are evidence, not source. The sibling PROVENANCE.md is prose and IS
# formatted, so only the payload is named here.
rust/crates/quoin-quire/tests/fixtures/coverage-volume/filament-ide-rs-coverage.json

# Canonical semantic-audit outputs are content-addressed evidence generated by
# scripts/semantic-module-type-fit.mjs. Reformatting them would invalidate the
# retained byte digests and make the formatter a second serialization authority.
analysis/semantic-module-type-fit/

# Corpus measurement outputs, on the same rule. `run-manifest.json` records a
# sha256 for each sibling document it was produced with, so reformatting any of
# them makes the manifest describe bytes that no longer exist.
analysis/corpus-measurement/

# Canonical change-assurance CLI goldens (FR-068 AC-10). These are the exact
# JCS bytes the commands emit and a consumer stores; the compatibility claim is
# byte identity, so a formatter that re-indents them turns the golden into a
# second serialization authority and the drift check into a tautology. Same
# reasoning as the vendored quire schemas and the captured tool output above.
tests/fixtures/change-assurance-cli/

# Vendored semantic-module contract schemas (quoin FR-070/073/075, issue #293):
# the filament-core-service module-manifest schema, the semantic-core JSON
# Schema bundle, and filament-core-data's package-manifest/common schemas. Same
# rule as src/quire/schemas/: provenance and sha256 are recorded in
# src/semantic/contract.ts and asserted on every test run; refresh with
# scripts/refresh-manifest-schema.mjs and
# scripts/refresh-semantic-core-schemas.mjs, never with prettier.
src/semantic/schemas/
tests/fixtures/semantic-module/

# The semantic-module cookiecutter (quoin FR-076, issue #307). Its files are
# Git worktrees of this same repository. Their tracked files are already
# linted from the root checkout; scanning them again double-lints and drags
# ignored template syntax back in. Git itself ignores .worktrees/.
.worktrees/

# Jinja templates, not JavaScript, TypeScript, JSON or YAML: prettier parses
# `{{ cookiecutter.x }}` inside a JSON value as a syntax error and rewrites
# `{%- if -%}` blocks into something cookiecutter no longer renders. The
# rendered repository formats ITSELF — `make format` in the generated tree runs
# black and ruff — which is where formatting belongs.
templates/semantic-module/

# The ajv-parity golden corpus (issue #378, EPIC #373 Stage 3). Produced once by
# scripts/capture-semantic-goldens.mjs from the TypeScript oracle — both deleted
# at the quoin#452 cutover per FR-101-AC-5 — each file
# carrying the quoin revision it was captured at. The contract is "regenerate,
# never hand-edit": a formatter re-indenting them makes the committed bytes
# differ from what the producer emits, so the next regeneration reads as a
# change that nobody made. Same rule as the vendored schemas above — these bytes
# are evidence, not source.
rust/crates/quoin-semantic/tests/goldens/
rust/crates/quoin-completeness/tests/goldens/

# The quoin#377 golden oracle (rust/crates/quoin-validators). `expected.json` is
# captured output, not source: `tools/generate-oracle.mts` compares the bytes it
# re-derives from the retained TypeScript against this file exactly, so a
# formatter that re-indents it makes the reproduction check fail against a file
# nothing produced. Same rule as src/quire/schemas/ and the change-assurance
# goldens above. `cases.json` beside it is hand-authored input and IS formatted.
rust/crates/quoin-validators/tests/golden/expected.json

# The quoin#447 golden oracle (rust/crates/quoin-assurance), on the same rule as
# the quoin#377 one above, with one difference: its subject is GONE. It was
# captured from `src/assurance/` in the commit before that directory was
# deleted, and its generator was deleted alongside it, so nothing here can
# re-derive these bytes any more — the Rust replays assert against them
# directly. That makes the no-formatting rule stricter rather than looser: a
# re-indent would silently rewrite the only surviving record of what the
# TypeScript answered. See the crate's tests/golden/PROVENANCE.md for the
# revision and the file hashes that make it checkable.
# `cases.json` beside it is hand-authored input and IS formatted.
rust/crates/quoin-assurance/tests/golden/expected.json

# The quoin#456 adapter and store golden oracles (rust/crates/quoin-evidence),
